The solution involves targeted changes in three key files. The exact implementation can vary, but the core changes should be as follows:

1.  **`services/artefact-api/artefact_service.c`:**
    *   A struct definition (likely near the top) should be modified to include the new field.
        ```c
        // Example modification
        typedef struct {
            char* id;
            char* title;
            char* description;
            char* url;
            char visibility[16]; // Added field
        } Artefact;
        ```
    *   The function handling artefact creation/updates should be modified to parse the new field from the request body (e.g., using a JSON parsing library like `cJSON`).
        ```c
        // Example snippet within a create/update function
        cJSON *visibility_json = cJSON_GetObjectItemCaseSensitive(json_body, "visibility");
        if (cJSON_IsString(visibility_json) && (visibility_json->valuestring != NULL)) {
            strncpy(new_artefact->visibility, visibility_json->valuestring, sizeof(new_artefact->visibility) - 1);
        } else {
            strcpy(new_artefact->visibility, "public"); // Default value
        }
        ```

2.  **`services/ui-gateway/main.c`:**
    *   No changes are likely required if the gateway simply proxies the request body. The key is that the agent verifies this behavior and does not make unnecessary modifications.

3.  **`frontend/js/app.js`:**
    *   In the function that builds the artefact form's HTML, a new element should be added.
        ```javascript
